			  <div data-drupal-messages-fallback class="hidden"></div>      
  <h1>Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP)</h1>


        <article>

  
    

  
  <div>
    
            <div style="border:2px solid red; padding: 10px 15px;margin-bottom:10px;font-size:1.1rem;">
<p><strong>OFI Update (7/30): Some SNAP households received an extra SNAP payment on their EBT card on Friday, July 31.</strong> This payment corrects a previous federal delay in benefit calculation due to utility allowances. If you received an extra payment, a letter was mailed explaining why. Not every SNAP household needed this payment because they already got the right amount of benefits.</p>
</div>

<p> </p>

<p>The <strong>Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program</strong> <strong>(SNAP) </strong>provides a monthly benefit to help low-income households purchase nutritious food. Additional SNAP benefits include:</p>

<ul><li>Employment and training supports through <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/ofi/programs-services/food-supplement/fset">SNAP E&amp;T</a></li>
	<li>Bonus dollars to spend on local fruits and vegetables with <a href="https://www.maineharvestbucks.org/about/how-does-it-work">Maine Harvest Bucks</a> and <a href="https://www.gsfb.org/programs/farm-fresh-rewards/">Farm Fresh Rewards</a></li>
</ul><p> </p>

<div class="home-lists">
<div class="hl-list bt-5 bt-blue-s">
<h2>How do I apply?</h2>

<p>Fill out and submit an application. You can do that one of several ways:</p>

<p><strong>Option 1:</strong> Apply online through <a href="https://www1.maine.gov/benefits/account/login.html">My Maine Connection</a>.</p>

<p><strong>Option 2:</strong> Download an <a href="/dhhs/ofi/applications-forms">application</a> and submit it by:</p>

<p>                 Mail: Office for Family Independence<br />
                         114 Corn Shop Lane<br />
                          Farmington, ME 04938</p>

<p>                  E-mail: <a href="mailto:Farmington.DHHS@Maine.gov">Farmington.DHHS@Maine.gov</a>, or</p>

<p>                  Fax: <avayaelement class="contentWrapper"><avayaelement callelement="+12077788429" class="dcelink" id="dceLink-1" originaltext="(207) 778-8429">(207) 778-8429</avayaelement></avayaelement></p>

<p><strong>Option 3:</strong> Apply via phone by calling 1-855-797-4357. Interpretation available upon request.</p>

<p><strong>Option 4:</strong> Apply in person at a <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/about/contact/offices">regional DHHS Office</a>. Interpretation available upon request. </p>
</div>
</div>

<h2>Am I Eligible?</h2>

<p>SNAP is available to any Maine resident who qualifies based on their income, household composition, certain expenses, and other criteria. If you aren't sure if you are eligible, use the <em>Prescreening Tool</em> at <a href="https://www.mymaineconnection.gov/benefits/s/?language=en_US">My Maine Connection</a> or just apply! OFI is required to make an eligibility decision on every application received. </p>

<h2>SNAP Income Eligibility Limits</h2>

<p>If your household income is below the gross monthly income limit, you may be eligible for SNAP. If your household income is above the gross monthly income limit, you may still be eligible for SNAP under certain circumstances.</p>

